From: ctos research <noreply@ctos.local>
Subject: [PATCH] RESEARCH ONLY: hw/arm/virt: TYPE_NMI -> async SError sketch

WARNING: Research sketch for ADR-082 B1. NOT reviewed. NOT CI-wired.
NOT proven against a specific QEMU commit. May not compile on master
without retargeting GPIO / interrupt constants.

Intent: implement TYPE_NMI on virt so QMP inject-nmi raises async SError
on CPU0 (TCG), matching the 2020 "Simulate NMI Injection" direction
without claiming FEAT_NMI is SError.

Apply only under sponsor-approved pinned build + guest el0: serror proof.

---
This patch is intentionally incomplete as a reminder it is not production:

diff --git a/hw/arm/virt.c b/hw/arm/virt.c
index 0000000..deadbeef
--- a/hw/arm/virt.c
+++ b/hw/arm/virt.c
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
